Håvard

Thank you for the reply, and for all the work on the methodology INLA.

My question arose when I tried to compare the performance of the method with the INLA MCMC estimation presented in the article

"Bayesian Analysis of Stochastic Volatility Models" , Eric Jacquier, Nicholas G. Polson, Peter E. Rossi

Journal of Business & Economic Statistics, Vol 12, No. 4. (Oct. 1994), pp. 371-389.

Link - http://harrisd.net/papers/ARCHSV/Multivariate 20Stochastic%%% 20Volatility 20Models/JacquierPolsenRossi1994JoBES.pdf

In particular comparing the sampling experiment shown on page 383 with the estimation results using INLA, for some parameters the performance of the INLA is slightly worse than those obtained by the estimation by MCMC. The INLA results are below:

