> wgts = c(rep(1,m),rep(0,n+q))
> node=1:(m+n+q)
>
> formula= y ~ -1+x + f(node,wgts, model="rw2d", nrow=m1, ncol=m2
> +m2extra)
> mod=inla(formula,data=list(y=y,x=Xnew,node=node,wgts=wgts),E=E,control.predictor=list(A=Anew),family='Poisson')
>
> It's a bit of extra computation but you'll see that Anew*(beta*Xnew +
> fnew) = beta*X+A*f so it does what I need.
>
> Not sure if this situation is common enough that having the
> functionality to specify that A should be applied to only some of the
> components of the linear predictor would be useful to others.
>
> Chris

